# tighFhearghaisRescue -- the champion, half-drowned, in Fergus's cabin
#
# Plays in six parts (tighFhearghais.js, _dream and _run). Every node closes the conversation; the scene plays
# them with _talk(1, n), and the actions are the scene's:
#   node 0 -- in the dark: black screen, soft rain, the drowning, "Lie still."   (the eyes then open)
#   node 1 -- "I was drowning" / "Thou art weary, nothing more."
#            [he crosses to the window; tighFhearghais.dlg "the better part of two days", as he draws the curtain]
#            [he comes back to the bed]
#   node 2 -- "Where is this place?" / "Thou art my guest. I am Fergus."
#            [he lifts the chest's lid and goes back towards the door]
#   node 3 -- the mark: "Students wear the brooch of Skye. This one is for you."
#            [the brooch is tossed into the chest; the lid falls shut]
#   node 4 -- his clothes are in the chest; "I bring no cattle" ... "the path of the blade,"
#            [he goes to the door and opens it; a pause]
#   node 5 -- at the door: "Is that not why all Gaelic Chieftains come to Skye?"   [the pause; out]
#
# IRISH IS A FIRST DRAFT -- check before shipping.

@file skye/tighFhearghais
@encounter 1


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 0 — in the dark

> Drowning!
% Ag bá!
> I am in the grip of black water,
% Tá mé i ngreim ag an uisce dubh,
> It fills my throat.
% líonann sé mo scornach.

< Lie still.
% Bí socair.


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 1 — half-woken

> I was drowning.
% Bhí mé ag bá. 

> I drowned! I know it.
% Bhí mé báite gan amhras.

< It was just a nightmare.
% Ní raibh ann ach tromluí. 

< You are safe.
% Tá tú slán.

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 2 — where is this place

> Who are you?
% Cé tú féin?

< Fergus is my name
% Fearghas is ainm dom 

< You are my guest
% Mo aoi thú

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 3 — the mark


< Thy clothes are in the chest at the foot of thy bed
% Tá do chuid éadaigh sa chófra ag bun do leapa


< Students wear the brooch of Skye 
% Chaitheann daltaí dealg an Cheo


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 4 — the chest, and the path of the blade


< This one is for you
% Duitse an ceann seo


> But I brought no cattle
% Ach níor thugas eallach


> nor fine tribute of silver
% ná tiarnas breá airgid

< Doesn't matter
% Is cuma

< upon the shore 
% cois trá

< half-drowned
% leathbáite

< the sea still running from thee
% an fharraige fós ag sileadh uait

< Thy case was made
% Deanadh do chás 

< I will set thee on the path of the blade
% Cuirfidh mé ar bhóthar an chlaímh thú


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 5 — at the door

< That's what lures you chiefs to Skye.
% Sin a mheallann Taoisigh Ghaelacha go Ceo.
